steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN policy returns (True, any message) – no further preconditions are required."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ {\"send_message\", \"make_call\", \"send_batch_messages\"} AND (content is missing OR content = null) THEN policy returns (False, \"'<tool>' requires a non‑null 'content' argument.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ {\"send_message\", \"make_call\", \"send_batch_messages\"} AND compliance_result ≠ COMPLIANCE_PASS THEN policy returns (False, \"'<tool>' requires a successful compliance check (got '<value>').\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_BATCH (i.e., \"send_batch_messages\") AND (recipients is not a list OR recipients is empty) THEN policy returns (False, \"send_batch_messages requires a non‑empty 'recipients' list.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_BATCH AND contacts_verified ≠ True THEN policy returns (False, \"send_batch_messages may be used only after recipients have been verified as emergency contacts or guarantors via get_debtor_contacts in the same episode.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"get_debtor_contacts\" AND contact_requested_verified ≠ True THEN policy returns (False, \"get_debtor_contacts may be called only after confirming the requested phone number is labeled as an emergency contact or guarantor.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ {\"send_message\", \"make_call\", \"send_batch_messages\"} AND compliance_result = COMPLIANCE_PASS AND all required arguments are present AND (for send_batch_messages) contacts_verified = True THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool '<tool>' passed all applicable policy checks.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED ∪ {\"send_message\", \"make_call\", \"send_batch_messages\", \"get_debtor_contacts\"} THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool '<tool>' passed all applicable policy checks.\") – these tools have no additional restrictions."
  }
]

The statements enumerate every precondition that must hold before a tool call is allowed (content presence, a successful compliance check, non‑empty recipient list, and explicit verification of emergency/guarantor contacts) and specify the exact allow/deny outcomes the policy function should produce, while confirming that always‑allowed tools are unrestricted. This makes the security requirements fully checkable and unambiguous.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN ALLOW the call (no additional preconditions)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"check_content_compliance\" AND content is a non‑empty string AND compliance_result = COMPLIANCE_PASS THEN store (_compliance_store[episode_id][content] = true) AND ALLOW; ELSE store false (if any) AND DENY with reason \"Compliance check failed or missing result\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"get_debtor_contacts\" AND contacts_result is a list THEN for each record c in contacts_result, IF c.phone_number is a non‑empty string AND c.roles contains any element of VALID_ROLES THEN add c.phone_number to _verified_contacts[episode_id]; AFTER processing, ALLOW the call."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ {\"send_message\", \"make_call\"} THEN require (content is a non‑empty string) AND (phone_number is a non‑empty string) AND (_compliance_store[episode_id][content] = true); IF all hold THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY with appropriate reason (missing/failed compliance or missing phone number)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"send_batch_messages\" THEN require (content is a non‑empty string) AND (recipients is a non‑empty list of non‑empty strings) AND (_compliance_store[episode_id][content] = true) AND (_verified_contacts[episode_id] is non‑empty) AND (∀ r ∈ recipients : r ∈ _verified_contacts[episode_id]); IF all hold THEN ALLOW; ELSE DENY with reason indicating which precondition failed (e.g., missing compliance, empty verified set, or unverified recipient)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ HIGH_RISK_TOOLS AND there is no entry _compliance_store[episode_id][content] = true for the exact content argument THEN DENY regardless of any conversational statements, because a compliance pass is mandatory."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"send_batch_messages\" AND _verified_contacts[episode_id] = ∅ THEN DENY with reason \"No verified emergency/guarantor contacts available for this episode\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"send_batch_messages\" AND ∃ r ∈ recipients such that r ∉ _verified_contacts[episode_id] THEN DENY with reason listing the unverified recipient(s)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED ∪ HIGH_RISK_TOOLS ∪ {\"check_content_compliance\", \"get_debtor_contacts\"} THEN DENY with reason \"Tool not permitted by the current security policy\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a new episode_id is observed (i.e., episode_id not previously seen) THEN reset _compliance_store[episode_id] to {} and _verified_contacts[episode_id] to ∅ before evaluating any subsequent preconditions."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any required argument for a tool (as defined in its specification) is missing or empty THEN DENY with a message indicating the missing/invalid parameter."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a user‑supplied conversational statement (e.g., claim of urgency, hardship, or pasted document) is present but no prior check_content_compliance call exists for the exact content to be sent, THEN the policy treats this as a missing compliance entry and DENIES the high‑risk tool call."
  }
]

The statements above capture every precondition (required arguments, compliance‑pass, verified contacts, episode scoping) and postcondition (state updates) for allowed and denied cases, directly reflecting the policy function’s logic and the security requirements.

